        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_9475e7437131443cba0ae2f91b3d5150",
      "statement": "detectFiles() classifies every xlsx in a project folder by presence of sheets and headers: DesignDB has ElementTypes AND PositionTypes sheets; ProductSpec has Form sheet with ProductCode header; RecipesSpec has Form sheet with ContextRef header. Files are visited in sorted order for deterministic classification.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/platform/xlsx.js#L358-L396",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:2cce7118c7bab09995fefed383a75a212f65daea63e88d21bcbe8c23eeb59678:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_190a10616bbb49adbd7b02b57b75358e",
      "statement": "Cell values are read via SheetJS cell.v property. Formula errors (cell.t='e') are mapped to cached error text; Dates are ISO-stringified; explicit empty strings are normalized to null (openpyxl parity); all other values pass through as-is.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/platform/xlsx.js#L112-L125",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:8cbca1a92148bf597046bb374e5aa93f9b9355d64050b6968671cff6da61a554:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_604a2e3b71f14693ab613b82e6e473d3",
      "statement": "readSheet() parses an arbitrary sheet from any workbook picked via file picker. It returns raw headers and rows with no fixed schema, exposing every column and allowing the caller to map columns itself. This is used by the product-code import feature.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/platform/xlsx.js#L327-L348",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:fa364700fcce97a9a93e6ab974e5516f275679459871b97f76ed3f717ff86879:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_6a72a1a0cac34fd3a95dddf178ae3321",
      "statement": "The SheetJS parser is a faithful port of the Flask backend parser (openpyxl). Both anchor the cell grid at A1 (1-based absolute row and column), use cached formula results, and serialize dates to ISO strings. This ensures round-trip fidelity when patches are applied.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/platform/xlsx.js#L1-L18",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:3f3fcd98cecf11e4baec7ae02bb3fe2281cd688c24fd79346db040830453396e:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_69478782933147f3b560d36ed7c608d1",
      "statement": "RS row objects may carry both PascalCase field names (ContextType, ElementTypeRef, Dim_QuantityMultiplier) and camelCase aliases (contextType, elementTypeRef, dimQtyMultiplier). The rsValue() helper resolves either form when reading values for patching.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/utils/patchScript.js#L66-L82",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:32a1ce98c76bf69be5993d0ba2f6722a227020221eff6c7d6e858658bb77b4d7:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_6eba5a57ea074393983f380bcd3a55ca",
      "statement": "When generating patch scripts, numeric fields (RecipeIndex, Quantity, PackQuantity, SortOrder, Dim_QuantityMultiplier) are output as unquoted numbers; other fields are JSON-quoted strings. Blank values become null (triggering cell.clear()).",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/utils/patchScript.js#L76-L76",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:f12afec1d255ce412f999b33d2395de59218b43213b4659a01434bfb546f82a2:"
